From e2bdd6f91917a4ab575c1d2659d810ff3d7a45c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:21:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] Trace rays with VK_KHR_ray_query instead of
 VK_KHR_ray_tracing_pipeline

Most Android GPUs (Adreno, Mali/Immortalis) expose ray queries but not
ray tracing pipelines. The path tracer now runs as compute shaders that
trace rays inline:

Shaders
- RtRaygen{Primary,ReflRefr,Direct,Indirect}.rgen -> .comp (8x8 groups)
- traceRayEXT -> rayQueryEXT loops in RaygenCommon.h; closest-hit and
  miss logic is inlined, so RtClsOpaque.rchit / RtMiss*.rmiss are gone
- the any-hit alpha test (RtAlphaTest.rahit) runs on each candidate
  triangle; only FORCE_NO_OPAQUE instances (the alpha-tested hit group)
  produce candidates, opaque instances are committed by the hardware
- shadow rays use TerminateOnFirstHit (same result as before)
- gl_LaunchIDEXT/SizeEXT -> gl_GlobalInvocationID + push constant size,
  with an early-out for invocations past the render size

Host
- RayTracingPipeline: 4 compute pipelines + push constant, no SBT
- PathTracer: rebinds its descriptor sets before each pass, as the
  denoiser and decal passes now share the compute bind point
- all barriers/descriptor stages: RAY_TRACING_SHADER -> COMPUTE_SHADER
  (incl. the TLAS build barrier, which only waited for ray tracing)
- device selection and creation: require rayQuery + accelerationStructure,
  drop ray tracing pipeline / pipeline library extensions
- requested features are masked by what the device supports; the ones the
  shaders/host really need are checked with a clear error
